---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead
      title="Apparatus"
      description="The analytical lens Blackwood applies across variable terrain. The domain is the substrate. The mechanism is the subject."
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header />
    <main>

      <h1 class="sr-only">Apparatus — Blackwood Intelligence</h1>

      <hr class="heavy" style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 3rem;" />

      <div class="apparatus-body">

        <p>The domain is the substrate. The mechanism is the subject.</p>

        <p>Blackwood applies a consistent analytical lens across variable terrain — finance, military history, institutional architecture, cognitive systems, competitive strategy. The surface content changes. The structural questions do not.</p>

        <p>Those questions concern how systems constrain themselves: through the incentive structures they generate, the information topologies they allow to form, the accountability distributions they embed, and the path dependencies their own past choices impose on future possibility. The inquiry is not what happened. It is what structural conditions made it likely.</p>

        <p>Four conditions recur across the work. How locally rational behavior generates globally irrational outcomes when actors optimize for their own segment without visibility into the full topology. How accumulated advantage recursively modifies the conditions under which further advantage becomes accessible — making dominance a function of trajectory rather than capability. How architectures of delay, in recognition, attribution, and loss realization, become the primary mechanism for absorbing stress until reversion becomes structurally impossible. How interpretive frameworks, once validated by accumulated experience, begin filtering reality rather than reading it.</p>

        <p>These are not four separate problems. They are four surfaces of the same condition: a system whose structure systematically produces outcomes inconsistent with its apparent design.</p>

        <p>That inconsistency is what Blackwood traces. The domain is always incidental.</p>

      </div>

    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  .apparatus-body {
    max-width: 58ch;
  }

  .apparatus-body p {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.0125rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.85;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .apparatus-body p:first-child {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .apparatus-body p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
</style>
